    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Midway was founded in the early 19th century as a stagecoach stop between Natchitoches and Shreveport, giving the town its name from its central location along the route.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/united-states/louisiana_midway"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s economy has long been rooted in timber and farming, making agriculture the primary industry in Midway.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/united-states/louisiana_midway"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Midway’s quiet countryside vibe offers a sharp contrast to Louisiana’s bustling cities, giving travelers a taste of rural life.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/united-states/louisiana_midway"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Geographically, Midway sits at 31.68° north latitude and 92.15° west longitude, placing it in northeastern Louisiana.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
